    ├── Pitfalls   : confluent-kafka uses librdkafka (C library) requiring system dependencies; Callback signatures differ: 
    │   confluent-kafka uses delivery_report(err, msg) vs kafka's add_callback/add_errback; confluent-kafka Producer.poll() must be 
    │   called periodically for callbacks to fire; kafka-python handles this internally; Configuration parameter names differ (e.g., 
    │   'bootstrap.servers' vs 'bootstrap_servers')
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The code uses kafka.KafkaProducer for synchronous message production with callback-based async handling. confluent-kafka 
        provides a compatible Producer API with similar send/flush semantics and callback support, making it a viable drop-in 
        replacement for the same synchronous producer role.

