└── async concurrency runtime (greenlet-based)
    ├── Candidates : gevent, eventlet
    ├── Used APIs  : monkey.patch_all
    ├── Pitfalls   : eventlet has different greenlet scheduling behavior; some C extensions may not patch cleanly; eventlet is less 
    │   actively maintained than gevent; monkey.patch_all() must be called before any other imports in both cases
    └── gevent is used only for monkey.patch_all() to patch stdlib for cooperative concurrency. eventlet provides the same 
        monkey-patching API and is a well-known drop-in alternative for this pattern. Both are greenlet-based runtimes used to make 
        Flask-SocketIO work with synchronous-looking code.

